problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set $$\mathcal{P}$$ of protein options and a finite set $$\mathcal{V}$$ of vegetable options, with items indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{P}$$ and $$j \in \mathcal{V}$$.
- Each protein option has a unit price coefficient $$c_i$$ measured per $$100$$ grams.
- Each vegetable option has a unit price coefficient $$c_j$$ measured per $$100$$ grams and a fiber coefficient $$f_j$$ measured per $$100$$ grams.
- The meal must use a total amount of food equal to $$Q$$ grams.
- The total purchase cost must stay within a budget limit of $$B$$.
- Exactly one protein option must be selected from $$\mathcal{P}$$.
- At least $$K$$ distinct vegetable options must be selected from $$\mathcal{V}$$.
- Food quantities may be purchased only for selected items; unselected items must have zero purchased quantity.
- The planning goal is to maximize total fiber intake while satisfying the budget, total mass, and category-selection rules.
- A solution is represented by:
  - purchased quantity variables $$x_i$$ for each protein option $$i \in \mathcal{P}$$ and $$x_j$$ for each vegetable option $$j \in \mathcal{V}$$, measured in grams;
  - binary selection variables $$y_i$$ for each protein option $$i \in \mathcal{P}$$ and $$y_j$$ for each vegetable option $$j \in \mathcal{V}$$, indicating whether the item is included in the meal;
  - an optimal fiber value representing the best achievable total fiber intake.

Input Format
{
  "proteins": {
    "type": "array",
    "length": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
    "items": {
      "name": "string",
      "price_per_100g": "$$c_i$$"
    }
  },
  "vegetables": {
    "type": "array",
    "length": "$$|\\mathcal{V}|$$",
    "items": {
      "name": "string",
      "price_per_100g": "$$c_j$$",
      "fiber_per_100g": "$$f_j$$"
    }
  },
  "budget": "$$B$$",
  "total_mass_grams": "$$Q$$",
  "min_selected_vegetable_types": "$$K$$"
}

Output Format
{
  "proteins": {
    "type": "array",
    "length": "$$|\\mathcal{P}|$$",
    "items": {
      "name": "string",
      "selected": "$$y_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$$",
      "quantity_grams": "$$x_i \\ge 0$$"
    }
  },
  "vegetables": {
    "type": "array",
    "length": "$$|\\mathcal{V}|$$",
    "items": {
      "name": "string",
      "selected": "$$y_j \\in \\{0,1\\}$$",
      "quantity_grams": "$$x_j \\ge 0$$"
    }
  },
  "total_fiber": "$$Z^\\star$$",
  "total_cost": "$$C^\\star$$",
  "total_mass_grams": "$$Q$$"
}

